Z||000005||terryk||04-06-2000||02:12 AM||||92 and up Dustbuster vans (U body) have the 4T60E/3800NA with 3:43 final drives (at least that what the note I have here says). The other C/H cars are 2.84, 3.06, and 3.33. Various gear combo's give 2.97, 3.06 and 3.33 overall. <P>All limiters for the rev and speed are in the ECM calibration. Nothing in the transmission. I play with the 92-95 SC's. In my 92/93 code, the rev limiter is 5600/5100 On/off in drive and 6000/6000 in P/N. To limit the speed, 3 degrees of spark is removed for every mile per hour above 112 MPH. This effectively soft limits. The car just stops pulling. In 94/95 they add a few other things. Also, there is ABM (abusive manuever mode). Things like "He's not moving, the brake is applied, the RPM's are up at 2200 RPM. I wonder what he's planning?. Let's pull some spark and save the transmission." Or "Park, 3000 RPM, shifter changes to Drive". Let's pull LOTS OF SPARK!!!!!!!!<P>I disabled this (the engine and trans is in an 86 Ciera GT at 3060 lbs) and I hit 141MPH before I starting thinking about all of the bolts I probably forgot to tighten and let off. It *might* have hit 150, but it was certainly not pulling that hard. A slow creep up. <P>The issue with the 4T6xE trans is the 2-3 shifts. If they are going to die, it's then.<BR>The cheese grater explodes. The engine torque is limited most during that period via advance reduction. They do it via tubine shaft torque calculations not engine torque.<BR>||||reg||1
